name cm-beam-only-1
timeout 200

# THE COUNTERMEASURE EXPERIMENT, LEG 3 OF FOUR. Four missions share ONE geometry and ONE shot and
# differ in exactly two bits — does the bandit MANOEUVRE across the shot, and does it THROW CHAFF — so
# that the four closest-approach numbers are a 2x2 table and not four anecdotes:
#
#     cm-straight-clean.fbm   head-on, no chaff   the reference: what this shot does undisturbed
#     cm-chaff-straight.fbm   head-on, chaff      chaff alone
#     cm-beam-only.fbm        beaming, no chaff   the manoeuvre alone
#     cm-chaff-beam.fbm       beaming, chaff      both
#
# THE SHOT, identical in all four: the viper flies EAST from 46.900/6.900 at 8,000 m with the ACM HUD box
# open to 40 nm, locks the bandit 25 km ahead and pickles at t=10 s. One AIM-120, briefed release, no
# manoeuvring by the shooter.
#
# THE PHYSICS THE TABLE IS ABOUT (systems/FBRadarSystem::kDopplerNotchMs): a chaff cloud has no velocity
# of its own, so a pulse-Doppler seeker rejects it as clutter — UNLESS the aircraft it is tracking is
# itself crossing the line of sight, because then the target's own radial velocity is in the same
# Doppler filter as the cloud's and the processor has no way to prefer one over the other. Chaff without
# the manoeuvre is therefore rejected, the manoeuvre without chaff leaves the seeker nothing to be
# confused BY, and only the two together take the round off the target.
#
# THIS LEG flies the beam manoeuvre and throws nothing: the bandit is already on a 350 deg heading at
# spawn, i.e. the shot is taken ACROSS it from the start, and the shooter sits on its 3/9 line for the
# whole engagement. The round has to solve a crossing intercept, which costs it accuracy — but with
# nothing else in its beam there is nothing for the notch to matter about.
#
# THE 2x2, as it stands after the missile-guidance round (closest approach, `stores DETONATION`):
#   clean 0.47 m hit | chaff only 0.47 m hit | BEAM ONLY 7.83 m HIT | chaff + beam: no detonation.
# This leg used to run past the target without a detonation at all; the terminal loop's conditional
# integration is what turned the crossing intercept back into a hit, and the table now says exactly
# what the physics above claims — only the two TOGETHER take the round off. Exit 1 (the bandit's
# decisive FAIL) was therefore this leg's expected outcome until 2026-07-29.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-29 after the spawn-tick frame fix (doc/sensors.md 10, item 24). This leg was the
# 2x2's marginal cell all along and it has now crossed: closest approach 7.83 -> 9.94 m against the 10 m
# fuze. The round still detonates, the damage no longer mission-kills, the bandit completes its route,
# and the exit moves 1 -> 0. THE TABLE'S STATEMENT IS UNCHANGED IN DIRECTION and weaker in strength:
#   clean 0.47 m | chaff only 0.47 m | BEAM ONLY 9.94 m (detonation, no kill) | chaff + beam: none.
# The beam manoeuvre alone now costs the round its kill rather than only its accuracy, which sharpens
# rather than contradicts the claim; what the leg can no longer carry is the word "hit".

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.90000 8000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 3 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 10                   # ~20 km, inside the launch zone, nothing else briefed
  wp 46.90000 7.15000 8000 400

unit bandit
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.20000 8000 350.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set cmds_mode off                        # the dispenser stays cold: nothing is ever thrown
  wp 47.25381 7.10756 8000 400             # 350 deg: across the shot, the shooter on the 3/9 line
